of  the  disk.   If that partition is used for a file system, the
user is responsible for making sure that it does not overlap  the
bad  sector  information  or  any replacement sectors.  Thus, one
track plus 126 sectors must be reserved to allow use  of  all  of
the  possible  bad sector replacements.  The bad sector structure
