On  an  11/750,  the  standard bootstrap drivers used to boot the
system do not understand bad sectors, handle errors, or the  spe‐
cial  (skip  sector)  errors of RM80‐type disks.  This means that
none of these errors can occur when reading  the  file  to  boot.
Sectors  0‐15  of  the disk drive must also not have any of these
errors.  The drivers which write a system core image on disk  af‐
ter  a  crash do not handle errors; thus the crash dump area must
be free of errors and bad sectors.
